# The files of format/ are read byte for byte: the line ends of a test vector are part of what it
# shows (module.plain-text), and the digest of a package is taken of a module's files as they are
# (format/README.md, sections 10 and 25). No checkout converts their line ends.
format/** -text
# The same holds for the fixtures of format-check's tests, which a trial copy of a format reads.
tools/format-check/test/fixtures/** -text
# The fixtures of release-verify's tests are files of real releases, which their bundles sign
# byte for byte.
tools/release/test/fixtures/** -text
# The API contracts are read byte for byte too: contracts-check holds each .proto file to what buf
# format writes and the generated code to what buf generates (R83), and so do the trial contracts
# of its tests.
contracts/** -text
tools/contracts/test/fixtures/** -text
